WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:17.392
"Maybe Molly was right," I thought when I got home.

2
00:00:17.393 --> 00:00:20.359
Maybe I was inventing stories.

3
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.991
Still I knew what I had heard.

4
00:00:22.992 --> 00:00:27.415
My mom had clearly said, "I'll have to rob a bank."

5
00:00:27.416 --> 00:00:29.718
I didn't invent that.

6
00:00:29.719 --> 00:00:35.594
I'd heard her say those words with my very own ears!

7
00:00:35.595 --> 00:00:40.910
Mom finally did serve dinner that night, but it was just cold sandwiches.

8
00:00:40.911 --> 00:00:44.676
And she definitely seemed worried about something.

9
00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:49.886
As we sat at the table eating, she stared off into space.

10
00:00:49.887 --> 00:00:54.992
"Mom, what are you thinking about?" I asked suddenly.

11
00:00:54.993 --> 00:00:58.527
"What?" she said, startled.

12
00:00:58.528 --> 00:01:00.668
I repeated my question.

13
00:01:00.669 --> 00:01:03.065
"What are you thinking about?"

14
00:01:03.066 --> 00:01:08.231
"I was just thinking about all the bills I have to pay," said Mom.

15
00:01:08.232 --> 00:01:11.148
My stomach did a little flip.

16
00:01:11.149 --> 00:01:13.434
"So you're really worried about money?"

17
00:01:13.435 --> 00:01:17.371
"Iggy, stop being weird," said Tate.

18
00:01:17.372 --> 00:01:20.019
My mother patted my hand.

19
00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:25.335
"You should be thinking about homework, Iggy, not bills," she said.

20
00:01:25.336 --> 00:01:28.986
Then she quickly started talking about something else.

21
00:01:28.987 --> 00:01:33.282
I got up early the next day to walk to school with Josh.

22
00:01:33.283 --> 00:01:41.285
He likes to get there early, and this morning I needed to talk to him.

23
00:01:41.286 --> 00:01:46.295
I got downstairs just as Josh was headed out the door.

24
00:01:46.296 --> 00:01:49.388
"Can I walk to school with you?" I asked.

25
00:01:49.389 --> 00:01:51.424
"I have something I want to tell you."

26
00:01:51.425 --> 00:01:54.223
"Sure," said Josh.

27
00:01:54.224 --> 00:01:56.149
"I'm worried about my mom,"

28
00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:59.094
I blurted out as we started walking.

29
00:01:59.095 --> 00:02:02.072
"Why?" asked Josh.

30
00:02:02.073 --> 00:02:04.733
"I think she needs money," I said.

31
00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:07.295
"She's worried about paying bills."

32
00:02:07.296 --> 00:02:11.119
"My dad worries about bills too," said Josh.

33
00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:14.911
We walked past the Green Apple Supermarket.

34
00:02:14.912 --> 00:02:18.686
That's where Josh and Jenny's dad works.

35
00:02:18.687 --> 00:02:24.621
He brings home lots of food for dinner, like steak and apple pie.

36
00:02:24.622 --> 00:02:29.027
So Josh didn't have to worry about having good dinners either!

37
00:02:29.028 --> 00:02:34.539
"My dad even works on the weekends, to make extra money for our family," Josh went on.

38
00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:36.550
"He performs magic shows.

39
00:02:36.551 --> 00:02:40.457
He's working on a new trick using a one-way mirror."

40
00:02:40.458 --> 00:02:43.829
"What's a one-way mirror?" I asked.

41
00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:47.742
"It's a mirror on one side," explained Josh.

42
00:02:47.743 --> 00:02:51.456
"But on the other side, you can see through it, like glass."

43
00:02:51.457 --> 00:02:54.374
"Oh," I said, nodding.

44
00:02:54.375 --> 00:02:59.900
I was pretty sure I'd seen mirrors like that on TV police shows.

45
00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:05.712
"Maybe I could invent a money-making machine," I said, thinking out loud.

46
00:03:05.713 --> 00:03:11.190
"I could print thousands of dollar bills, and then we'd be rich!"

47
00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.489
Josh stopped and looked at me.

48
00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:17.505
"Iggy, that's the worst idea in the world!"

49
00:03:17.506 --> 00:03:19.649
"Boy," I thought.

50
00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:24.207
"Josh either really likes an idea, or he really doesn't like it!"

51
00:03:24.208 --> 00:03:28.137
"What's wrong with a money-printing machine?" I asked him.

52
00:03:28.138 --> 00:03:31.576
"Printing money is a crime," said Josh.

53
00:03:31.577 --> 00:03:36.379
"If you invent a money-printing machine, you could go to jail!"

54
00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:38.793
"Jail?" I echoed.

55
00:03:38.794 --> 00:03:41.318
"Oh well. Forget that invention then."

56
00:03:41.319 --> 00:03:47.003
A second later Josh and I passed the candy store near school.

57
00:03:47.004 --> 00:03:52.430
My mouth watered as I looked at all the delicious candy.

58
00:03:52.431 --> 00:03:56.880
"I really wish I were rich now," I murmured.

59
00:03:56.881 --> 00:03:59.591
"Then I could buy this whole candy store!"

60
00:03:59.592 --> 00:04:02.698
I dug into my pocket and found some change.

61
00:04:02.699 --> 00:04:04.737
Josh had some too.

62
00:04:04.738 --> 00:04:09.281
Together, we had enough to buy a chocolate candy bar.

63
00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:12.281
We decided to save it for lunchtime.

64
00:04:12.282 --> 00:04:17.265
"If only I knew what my mom was thinking," I said as we walked on.

65
00:04:17.266 --> 00:04:19.202
"Then I would know what to do."

66
00:04:19.203 --> 00:04:20.846
Josh shook his head.

67
00:04:20.847 --> 00:04:22.904
"Grown-ups are pretty mysterious.

68
00:04:22.905 --> 00:04:26.618
You'd need a really great invention to figure them out!"

69
00:04:26.619 --> 00:04:30.948
That's when I got my greatest idea ever.

70
00:04:30.949 --> 00:04:35.870
"What if I could invent a magic thinking box?

71
00:04:35.871 --> 00:04:42.237
Then I'd be able to read people's thoughts!"
